    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A heavy double-bit axe on a long hickory haft, straight off the timber crews that keep the hex roads open. Nobody designed it as a weapon; nobody needed to. When the raid alarm sounds in a logging camp, this is what comes out of the shed.</p><p>Heavy two-handed chop. Honest work, either way.</p>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p>\n<p>Two-handed, heavy. Splits timber, doors and arguments. No signature ability.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d10 + 1 Kinetic damage to <em>Integrity</em> <span style=\"opacity:.75\">(chop)</span></li>\n  <li><strong>Faculty:</strong> Violence</li>\n  <li><strong>Attack:</strong> Melee (Violence)</li>\n  <li><strong>Reach:</strong> Melee</li>\n  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier:</strong> T2</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:END -->\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⟡ Inlaid (+1). Hex-inlay along the working edge.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>+1 to hit and +1 damage</strong> with this weapon (the hit bonus is read from the weapon you swing).</li>\n  <li>Grade raises it to <strong>Tier II</strong> · free to wield.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:END -->"
    }
  },
